          "turn_index": 1,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What is meant by secondary prevention?",
          "answer": "Secondary prevention refers to the actions taken for someone who has already been diagnosed with a condition, such as coronary artery disease, to reduce the likelihood of further events or worsening of the condition. It is not a single intervention but rather a combination of measures that work together to achieve this goal.\n\nFor example, in coronary artery disease, secondary prevention aims to reduce the chance of another heart attack or other related cardiac events. This concept is highlighted in the `guideline-coronary-artery-disease-secondary-prevention` document.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n[sources: guideline-coronary-artery-disease-secondary-prevention]",
          "risk_level": "routine",
